  "surface": "supplier_web",
  "riskClass": "high",
  "title": "BNPL orders hardcodes limit=100 with no pagination, silently truncates data for high-volume suppliers",
  "description": "R6 deep audit finding. Dimension: business-logic. Severity: P1. Source SHA: bbd487a3. Scope: R6_DEEP_AUDIT_WAVE. The fetchBnplOrders function hardcodes `params.set('limit', '100')` (line 42) and the page renders all results without any pagination controls. For suppliers with more than 100 BNPL-backed orders, the user never sees orders beyond the first 100 and has no way to discover this. Unlike other list pages (products, orders, invoices) which have pagination, BNPL orders silently truncates. There is no 'showing X of Y' indicator either.",
